  "name": "Question 15",
  "problem": "Let $V={R}_{2}[t]$ be the vector space of all polynomials of degree at most $2$, equipped with the inner product\n\n$$\n\u27e8x(t),y(t)\u27e9=x(1)y(1)+x(2)y(2)+x(3)y(3).\n$$\n\nFind $\u27e8x(t),y(t)\u27e9$, if\n\n$$\nx(t)={t}^{2}-2,\\,y(t)={t}^{2}+t.\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "Computing the inner product according to the definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u27e8x(t),y(t)\u27e9 & =x(1)y(1)+x(2)y(2)+x(3)y(3) \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot 2+2\\cdot 6+7\\cdot 12 \\\\  & =-2+12+84 \\\\  & =94.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
